    "body": "Currently, V8 takes the spec literally, so `console.log(\"%s%s\", \"wat%s\", \"wat\")` prints `watwat%s`. Spidermonkey follows the natural printf-like semantics and prints `wat%swat`. Node also prints `wat%swat`, despite being V8-based, because it brings its own `console` implementation. I am very much in favor of changing the spec to avoid this recursive behavior.",
